<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    ROADMAP.md Phase 3 — navigation skeleton for Onboarding, Consent & Interaction Spec §1's
    nine-screen sequence:
        1. Welcome / Product Philosophy         (§2.1)
        2. Goal Definition                       (§2.2)
        3. Tier Explanation                      (§2.3)
        4. Tier Selection                        (§2.4)
           -> if Iron selected: Iron Calibration Gate (§2.5 / PRD §12.6)
        5. Mission Profile Setup                 (§2.8)
        6. Core Data Consent                     (§2.6)
        7. Unsupervised Reliability Opt-In       (§2.7)
        8. First Mission Scheduling              (§2.9)

    Every destination currently points at OnboardingPlaceholderFragment (see that class's
    kdoc for why: nav-graph structure verified in isolation before any real screen content is
    built on top of it, matching this project's incremental-slice discipline) — EXCEPT
    welcomeFragment, goalDefinitionFragment, tierExplanationFragment, tierSelectionFragment,
    tierConfirmationFragment, and missionProfileSetupFragment, which have real content as of
    this session or a prior one (see each Fragment class's own kdoc).
    Real screens replace the remaining placeholders one at a time; the graph's structure
    (destination IDs, action IDs, the Tier-Selection branch) is the part meant to survive that
    replacement unchanged, since other Fragments will navigate by action ID, not by re-deriving
    the sequence each time.

    **As of this pass:** unsupervisedReliabilityOptInFragment and firstMissionSchedulingFragment
    also have real content now (UnsupervisedReliabilityOptInFragment,
    FirstMissionSchedulingFragment respectively) — see each destination's own comment below.
    Only ironCalibrationGateFragment remains OnboardingPlaceholderFragment; see row 4b's own
    note on why that's a deliberate, currently-correct state rather than a gap.

    **Iron branch status, updated:** the "known simplification" this comment used to describe
    (Tier Selection had no real tier-choice logic, so neither action from it was ever truly
    conditional) is now only half true. TierSelectionFragment's Iron RadioButton is disabled
    (§12.6, no exception path) — Iron genuinely cannot be chosen here, not just "not yet
    wired." Warden correctly routes through tierConfirmationFragment before ever calling
    selectInitialTier(). The one thing still not real: action_tierSelection_to_ironCalibrationGate
    remains unreachable from any code path, same as before — not because the branch logic is
    unbuilt, but because Iron is categorically unavailable at first-time onboarding by design,
    so there is currently no user-facing route that should ever fire this specific action.
    Left in the graph (rather than removed) because the destination and action still need to
    exist for whatever later flow lets an *existing* user reach Iron once their calibration
    window elapses (TierTransitionUseCase.activateIron, already built and tested — see
    ROADMAP.md Phase 1) — that flow was, until this pass, a Tier Selection *outside*
    onboarding this graph didn't model at all.

    **That flow now exists, added this pass, in this same graph:** firstMissionSchedulingFragment
    (destination 8 above) now has a real outgoing action to a new homeFragment destination —
    the minimum post-onboarding "onboarding complete" hand-off screen this file's own comment
    used to say didn't exist. From there, a new ironCalibrationFragment destination is the
    real activateIron() call site. Both are new, separate from the nine onboarding screens
    above and from ironCalibrationGateFragment specifically (still an unreachable-by-design
    placeholder, unchanged) — see homeFragment/ironCalibrationFragment's own comments below
    and each Fragment class's kdoc for the full reasoning.
-->
<navigation xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    xmlns:app="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res-auto"
    android:id="@+id/onboarding_nav_graph"
    app:startDestination="@id/welcomeFragment">

    <!-- 1. Welcome / Product Philosophy — §2.1. Real content as of this pass:
         WelcomeFragment replaces OnboardingPlaceholderFragment here. No title/stepNumber/
         totalSteps arguments, same reasoning as every other real-content destination in this
         graph (goalDefinitionFragment, tierSelectionFragment, etc.) dropping them — this
         Fragment has real layout content instead of the placeholder's generic step-progress
         mechanism. -->
    <fragment
        android:id="@+id/welcomeFragment"
        android:name="com.disciplineos.app.onboarding.WelcomeFragment"
        android:label="Welcome / Product Philosophy">
        <action
            android:id="@+id/action_welcome_to_goalDefinition"
            app:destination="@id/goalDefinitionFragment" />
    </fragment>

    <!-- 2. Goal Definition — §2.2. Real content as of this pass: GoalDefinitionFragment
         replaces OnboardingPlaceholderFragment here. No title/stepNumber/totalSteps
         arguments, same reasoning as missionProfileSetupFragment/tierSelectionFragment
         dropping them when they got real content — this Fragment has real layout content
         instead of the placeholder's generic step-progress mechanism. -->
    <fragment
        android:id="@+id/goalDefinitionFragment"
        android:name="com.disciplineos.app.onboarding.GoalDefinitionFragment"
        android:label="Goal Definition">
        <action
            android:id="@+id/action_goalDefinition_to_tierExplanation"
            app:destination="@id/tierExplanationFragment" />
    </fragment>

    <!-- 3. Tier Explanation — §2.3, "highest-stakes copy in onboarding". Real content as of
         this pass: TierExplanationFragment replaces OnboardingPlaceholderFragment here. No
         title/stepNumber/totalSteps arguments, same reasoning as every other real-content
         destination in this graph. -->
    <fragment
        android:id="@+id/tierExplanationFragment"
        android:name="com.disciplineos.app.onboarding.TierExplanationFragment"
        android:label="Tier Explanation">
        <action
            android:id="@+id/action_tierExplanation_to_tierSelection"
            app:destination="@id/tierSelectionFragment" />
    </fragment>

    <!-- 4. Tier Selection — §2.4. Real content as of this session: TierSelectionFragment
         replaces OnboardingPlaceholderFragment here. Recruit/Operator submit directly;
         Warden routes through the new Tier Confirmation screen first; Iron's RadioButton is
         disabled in the layout (§12.6, no exception path) so it can never be selected here at
         all — the Iron Calibration Gate destination below stays unreached from this pass,
         same as it was under the placeholder (see that destination's own comment). -->
    <fragment
        android:id="@+id/tierSelectionFragment"
        android:name="com.disciplineos.app.onboarding.TierSelectionFragment"
        android:label="Tier Selection">
        <action
            android:id="@+id/action_tierSelection_to_tierConfirmation"
            app:destination="@id/tierConfirmationFragment" />
        <action
            android:id="@+id/action_tierSelection_to_ironCalibrationGate"
            app:destination="@id/ironCalibrationGateFragment" />
        <action
            android:id="@+id/action_tierSelection_to_missionProfileSetup"
            app:destination="@id/missionProfileSetupFragment" />
    </fragment>

    <!-- Tier Confirmation — §2.4's "distinct confirmation screen" form of the Warden/Iron
         secondary-confirmation requirement. Only Warden routes here in this pass (Iron is
         rejected one screen earlier, at Tier Selection itself, before it could ever reach a
         confirmation step) — see TierConfirmationFragment's kdoc for why the class is still
         written to be extendable to Iron's own confirmation later without restructuring. -->
    <fragment
        android:id="@+id/tierConfirmationFragment"
        android:name="com.disciplineos.app.onboarding.TierConfirmationFragment"
        android:label="Confirm Tier">
        <argument
            android:name="tier"
            app:argType="string"
            android:defaultValue="WARDEN" />
        <action
            android:id="@+id/action_tierConfirmation_to_missionProfileSetup"
            app:destination="@id/missionProfileSetupFragment" />
    </fragment>

    <!-- Iron Calibration Gate — §2.5 / PRD §12.6. Conditional: only reached if Iron was
         selected at Tier Selection. Converges back to Mission Profile Setup, same as the
         non-Iron path — the calibration window doesn't change what comes after it in the
         onboarding sequence itself, per §1's flow diagram. -->
    <fragment
        android:id="@+id/ironCalibrationGateFragment"
        android:name="com.disciplineos.app.onboarding.OnboardingPlaceholderFragment"
        android:label="Iron Calibration Gate">
        <argument android:name="title" app:argType="string" android:defaultValue="Iron Calibration Gate" />
        <argument android:name="stepNumber" app:argType="integer" android:defaultValue="4" />
        <argument android:name="totalSteps" app:argType="integer" android:defaultValue="8" />
        <action
            android:id="@+id/action_ironCalibrationGate_to_missionProfileSetup"
            app:destination="@id/missionProfileSetupFragment" />
    </fragment>

    <!--
        5. Mission Profile Setup — §2.8 (first allowlist/blocklist). Real content as of this
        pass — see MissionProfileSetupFragment's own kdoc. No `title`/`stepNumber`/`totalSteps`
        arguments (those were OnboardingPlaceholderFragment's own mechanism for a generic
        screen to render step-progress text); this Fragment has real layout content instead,
        matching how tierSelectionFragment/tierConfirmationFragment dropped those same
        placeholder-only arguments when they got real content.
    -->
    <fragment
        android:id="@+id/missionProfileSetupFragment"
        android:name="com.disciplineos.app.onboarding.MissionProfileSetupFragment"
        android:label="Mission Profile Setup">
        <action
            android:id="@+id/action_missionProfileSetup_to_coreDataConsent"
            app:destination="@id/coreDataConsentFragment" />
    </fragment>

    <!-- 6. Core Data Consent — §2.6, required (not optional like the next screen). Real
         content as of this pass: CoreDataConsentFragment replaces OnboardingPlaceholderFragment
         here. No title/stepNumber/totalSteps arguments, same reasoning as every other
         real-content destination in this graph. -->
    <fragment
        android:id="@+id/coreDataConsentFragment"
        android:name="com.disciplineos.app.onboarding.CoreDataConsentFragment"
        android:label="Core Data Consent">
        <action
            android:id="@+id/action_coreDataConsent_to_unsupervisedReliabilityOptIn"
            app:destination="@id/unsupervisedReliabilityOptInFragment" />
    </fragment>

    <!-- 7. Unsupervised Reliability Opt-In — §2.7, "separate screen, genuinely optional".
         PRD §13.4 hard rule: must never be bundled into Core Data Consent above — kept as its
         own distinct destination for exactly that reason, not merged for convenience. Real
         content as of this pass: UnsupervisedReliabilityOptInFragment replaces
         OnboardingPlaceholderFragment here. No title/stepNumber/totalSteps arguments, same
         reasoning as every other real-content destination in this graph — this Fragment has
         real layout content instead of the placeholder's generic step-progress mechanism.
         Both Enable and Skip resolve to the same single outgoing action below, matching PRD
         §13.4's "declining does not gate access to any other feature." -->
    <fragment
        android:id="@+id/unsupervisedReliabilityOptInFragment"
        android:name="com.disciplineos.app.onboarding.UnsupervisedReliabilityOptInFragment"
        android:label="Unsupervised Reliability Opt-In">
        <action
            android:id="@+id/action_unsupervisedReliabilityOptIn_to_firstMissionScheduling"
            app:destination="@id/firstMissionSchedulingFragment" />
    </fragment>

    <!-- 8. First Mission Scheduling — §2.9, closes onboarding. Real content as of this pass:
         FirstMissionSchedulingFragment replaces OnboardingPlaceholderFragment here. No
         title/stepNumber/totalSteps arguments, same reasoning as every other real-content
         destination in this graph.

         **Now has an outgoing action, added this pass.** Previously this destination declared
         none at all (see this comment's own prior wording: "no real 'onboarding complete'
         hand-off screen yet, and this Fragment does not invent one") — STATUS.md's "what's
         actually next" item 2 named this exact gap. homeFragment below is that hand-off
         screen: the minimum real post-onboarding destination (see HomeFragment's own kdoc for
         scope — not a full dashboard). FirstMissionSchedulingFragment itself is unchanged; it
         still only creates the Mission row, navigating onward afterward is new. -->
    <fragment
        android:id="@+id/firstMissionSchedulingFragment"
        android:name="com.disciplineos.app.onboarding.FirstMissionSchedulingFragment"
        android:label="First Mission Scheduling">
        <action
            android:id="@+id/action_firstMissionScheduling_to_home"
            app:destination="@id/homeFragment"
            app:popUpTo="@id/onboarding_nav_graph"
            app:popUpToInclusive="true" />
    </fragment>

    <!-- Home — added this pass. Did not exist anywhere in this app before. See
         HomeFragment/HomeScreen's own kdoc for full reasoning: the minimum real
         post-onboarding destination, hosting the one concrete thing this pass was asked to
         build (a real entry point into Iron Calibration for a user who finished onboarding at
         a lower tier), not a full dashboard. Reached via popUpTo above — the entire
         onboarding back-stack is cleared on arrival, matching "onboarding is done, this is a
         new section of the app"; pressing Back from Home should not return into onboarding. -->
    <fragment
        android:id="@+id/homeFragment"
        android:name="com.disciplineos.app.home.HomeFragment"
        android:label="Home">
        <action
            android:id="@+id/action_home_to_ironCalibration"
            app:destination="@id/ironCalibrationFragment" />
        <action
            android:id="@+id/action_home_to_missionDetail"
            app:destination="@id/missionDetailFragment" />
    </fragment>

    <!-- Iron Calibration — added this pass. The real "existing user reaches Iron later via
         TierTransitionUseCase.activateIron" flow that ironCalibrationGateFragment's own
         comment (above) already described as unmodeled. Deliberately a separate destination
         from ironCalibrationGateFragment, not a repurposing of it — see
         IronCalibrationFragment's own kdoc for why. Only reachable from homeFragment. -->
    <fragment
        android:id="@+id/ironCalibrationFragment"
        android:name="com.disciplineos.app.home.IronCalibrationFragment"
        android:label="Iron Calibration" />

    <!-- Mission Detail — Batch G4 (Integration Plan §5/§7.6). The real entry point this
         section names explicitly: nothing before G4 lets a user reach a GoalMission's detail
         screen at all. Reached only from homeFragment's new Mission list — see HomeScreen's
         own comment on that list for why it lives on Home rather than a separate destination
         (Integration Plan §7.6's own stated resolution). missionId is a String argument (a
         serialized UUID, matching this graph's existing "primitive argType, parsed at the
         Fragment boundary" pattern — tierConfirmationFragment's own `tier` argument does the
         same for its enum instead of inventing a custom NavType for a one-destination need).

         **New outgoing action, Batch G5:** action_missionDetail_to_triggerCreation, added this
         pass — the "attach a Trigger?" prompt (base doc §4.3/Integration Plan §6) and any
         direct "add another trigger" action both navigate here. -->
    <fragment
        android:id="@+id/missionDetailFragment"
        android:name="com.disciplineos.app.mission.MissionDetailFragment"
        android:label="Mission Detail">
        <argument
            android:name="missionId"
            app:argType="string" />
        <action
            android:id="@+id/action_missionDetail_to_triggerCreation"
            app:destination="@id/triggerCreationFragment" />
    </fragment>

    <!-- Trigger Creation — Batch G5 (Integration Plan §6, base doc §3.4/§4.3). Reached only
         from missionDetailFragment. missionId is a String argument, same convention as
         missionDetailFragment's own argument above — parsed at the Fragment boundary, not a
         custom NavType. -->
    <fragment
        android:id="@+id/triggerCreationFragment"
        android:name="com.disciplineos.app.mission.TriggerCreationFragment"
        android:label="Add a Trigger">
        <argument
            android:name="missionId"
            app:argType="string" />
    </fragment>

</navigation>
